# Grafana Explore

## Defaults

1. Discover metric/log label names before writing heavy queries.
2. Start with a short time range; widen only if needed.
3. Prefer `rate` then `sum` for counters; avoid high-cardinality dumps.
4. Cite the query and a short result summary — not megabytes of raw series.
5. Use datasource health / list tools when a query returns empty unexpectedly.
